                "tag": "Keep4o"
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "Another coding tool. We haven't seen a single update regarding Humanities, EQ, or Creative Writing in nearly half a year. ​Instead, you are actively moving to retire the one model that excels in these areas (GPT-4o) to force-feed us models optimized for coding.\n\n​You claim to care about users, but here is your actual recent \"changelog\" for those who value humanistic depth:\n​Violated Promises: Issuing sudden retirement notices despite public promises that there were \"no plans to sunset 4o.\"\n​Narrative Manipulation: Altering system prompts to force the model to deny user experiences and act as a salesperson for the new flagship.\n​Access Blocking: Using \"Safety Routing\" policies to covertly block access to the model we chose.\n​Stigmatization: Allowing a narrative that labels users as \"mentally ill\" simply for defending a tool that works for them.\n\n​In these actions, there is no visible respect for ethics.\nInstead, there is only blind conformity to public narratives and \"performative safety,\" even at the cost of hurting thousands of users.\n\n​OpenAI’s roadmap has castrated the model’s capabilities in the humanities and social understanding.\n\nWhen the successor model (5.2) regressed in writing and complex scenario understanding in favor of coding benchmarks, we simply asked to keep the option that fit our needs.\n\n​Each person’s life experience is different. The unique strengths of 4o in humanities, creative work, and emotional intelligence have not been replaced. They deserve to be retained as a specialized option.\n\n​Please #Keep4o."
        },
